module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.RecoveringMorphisms.AffineComparisonIsIso

/-!
# The existence half of Stacks 04I6

Let `X` and `Y` be schemes of a big étale site, with `Y` affine, and let `(g, g^♯)` be a morphism
of their small étale **locally** ringed topoi.  Then there is a morphism of schemes `f : X ⟶ Y`
with `(g, g^♯)` 2-isomorphic to `(f_{small}, f_{small}^♯)`, and it is unique.  That is
[Stacks Project, Tag 04I6], and this file closes it.

Everything else is already available: the comparison `g⁻¹h_V ⟶ h_{X ×_Y V}` of step (3) of the source's
proof together with its naturality in both variables, its iso-ness at every affine chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.affineRepresentableComparison`), the transport of the resulting isomorphism of
direct images from the affine charts to all charts along [Stacks Project, Tag 04HR], and the
assembly of a 2-isomorphism from an isomorphism of direct images plus the agreement of the two
structure maps.  What this file supplies is that last agreement — the `hcomm` hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.existsUnique_schemeHom_twoIso_of_affineRepresentableComparison`, which is the
source's closing paragraph.

## The closing paragraph needs no generation argument

The source argues that `g^♯` and `f_{small}^♯` agree because they agree on `B` by the construction
of `f` and on the coordinate functions `x_i` by the commutativity of the defining square, `Γ(V, ⊤)`
being generated by the `x_i` over `B`.  Here no such argument is needed, and the presentation does
not appear at all.  The reason is that the comparison was built out of
`AlgebraicGeometry.comparisonRingHom`, a ring homomorphism `Γ(V, ⊤) ⟶ Γ(U, ⊤)` defined at *every*
global function on `V` at once, rather than out of the `n` coordinates; so
`AlgebraicGeometry.comparisonSheafHom_comp_yoneda_elt` — the identity
`comparisonSheafHom ≫ β'_t = comparisonElt t`, which the coordinate case
`AlgebraicGeometry.comparisonSheafHom_comp_yoneda` is an instance of — already holds at arbitrary
`t`, and the agreement of the structure maps is exactly that identity read with
`comparisonSheafHom` moved across the comparison isomorphism.

Checking the agreement at the affine charts suffices because restriction of sheaves to the small
affine étale site is faithful, [Stacks Project, Tag 04HR]
(`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallAffineEtale.restriction`).  Nothing here produces a comparison at a
non-affine chart, and nothing here needs one: that would be cancellation on the left, which is
false — see the module documentation of
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/DenseSubsite/NatIsoTransport.lean`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.sectionsEquivOfIso_forgetFSharp` — the agreement of the two structure maps at
  one affine chart, on sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.forgetFSharp_comp_pushforwardIsoOfAffineRepresentableComparison` — the
  agreement of the two structure maps, i.e. the `hcomm` hypothesis, for any comparison datum whose
  components are the comparison `g⁻¹h_V ⟶ h_{X ×_Y V}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_schemeHom_twoIso_of_isLocallyRinged` — **the existence half of
  [Stacks Project, Tag 04I6]**, which is the form its consumers want: uniqueness
  upgrades it for free.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.existsUnique_schemeHom_twoIso_of_isLocallyRinged` — **[Stacks Project, Tag
  04I6]** in full.

## The affineness of `X` is not used

The source states the tag for `X` and `Y` both affine.  Only `Y` affine is needed: it is what makes
a morphism of schemes into `Y` the same thing as a ring map on global functions (the source's first
paragraph) and what makes the étale charts of `Y` carry standard presentations.  The source's use
of `X = Spec A` is only to identify `A` with `Γ(X_étale, 𝒪_X)`, and that identification holds for
any scheme, the terminal object of the small étale site being `X / X`
(`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.smallEtaleRingedSite_structureSheaf_obj_final`).  So the statements below
are more general than the tag.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 04I6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04I6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04HR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04HR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04LW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04LW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04IC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04IC)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite
open Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback Stacks.EtaleCohomology AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) {X Y : B.Scheme}
  (g : RingedToposHom
    (RingedSite.toRingedTopos (smallEtaleRingedSite B X.obj X.property))
    (RingedSite.toRingedTopos (smallEtaleRingedSite B Y.obj Y.property)))
  (f : X ⟶ Y)
  (hf : (B.inclusion.map f).appTop =
    g.globalSectionsMap (SmallEtale.finalIsTerminal B X.obj X.property)
      (SmallEtale.finalIsTerminal B Y.obj Y.property))
  [IsAffine Y.obj]

include hf in
/-- **The two structure maps agree at one affine chart, on sections.**  Let `V` be an affine étale
chart of `Y` and `e : g⁻¹h_V ≅ h_{X ×_Y V}` an isomorphism whose forward map is the
comparison of step (3).  Then the sections bijection
`MorphismOfTopoi.representableSectionsEquivOfIso` which `e` induces carries `g^♯(b)` to
`f_{small}^♯(b)`, for every global function `b` on `V`.

This is the source's closing paragraph at a single chart, and it holds at *every* `b` rather than
only on the base and the coordinate functions.  Read in the direction of
`MorphismOfTopoi.representableSectionsEquivOfIso_symm_apply` the claim is
`g^♯(b) = (inverseImageYonedaRingEquiv) (comparisonSheafHom ≫ β'_b)`, where `β'_b` is the Yoneda
morphism of `b` pulled back along the projection; the composite is
`AlgebraicGeometry.comparisonElt` at `b` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.comparisonSheafHom_comp_yoneda_elt`, and `comparisonElt` is by construction
what the ring identification sends `g^♯(b)` to. -/
theorem sectionsEquivOfIso_forgetFSharp (V : SmallEtale B Y.obj Y.property)
    [IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toScheme B Y.obj Y.property).obj V)]
    (e : g.toToposHom.inverseImage.obj
          ((SmallEtale.topology B Y.obj Y.property).yoneda.obj V) ≅
        (SmallEtale.topology B X.obj X.property).yoneda.obj
          ((smallEtaleBaseChange B f).obj V))
    (he : e.hom = comparisonSheafHom B g f hf V)
    (b : Γ((SmallEtale.toScheme B Y.obj Y.property).obj V, ⊤)) :
    MorphismOfTopoi.representableSectionsEquivOfIso g.toToposHom
        ((RingedSite.toRingedTopos (smallEtaleRingedSite B X.obj X.property)).forgetRing.obj
          (RingedSite.toRingedTopos (smallEtaleRingedSite B X.obj X.property)).O)
        (u := smallEtaleBaseChange B f) e
        ((RingedToposHom.forgetFSharp g).hom.app (op V) b) =
      (RingedToposHom.forgetFSharp (smallEtaleRingedToposHom B f)).hom.app (op V) b := by
  refine (Equiv.apply_eq_iff_eq_symm_apply _).2 ?_
  show (g.fSharp.hom.app (op V)).hom b =
    (SmallEtale.topology B Y.obj Y.property).yonedaEquiv
      (g.toToposHom.adj.homEquiv _ _
        (e.hom ≫
          ((SmallEtale.topology B X.obj X.property).yonedaEquiv
            (F := Sheaf.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingSheaf B X.property))).symm
            ((SmallEtale.baseChangeProj B f V).appTop.hom b)))
  rw [he, comparisonSheafHom_comp_yoneda_elt B g f hf V b]
  exact ((MorphismOfTopoi.inverseImageYonedaRingHom_apply g.toToposHom
    (smallEtaleRingSheaf B X.property) V (comparisonElt B X.property Y.property g V b)).symm.trans
      ((inverseImageHomRingEquiv B X.property Y.property g V).apply_symm_apply
        ((g.fSharp.hom.app (op V)).hom b))).symm

include hf in
/-- **The agreement of the two structure maps: the `hcomm` hypothesis of Stacks 04I6, discharged.**
For any comparison datum at the affine charts whose components are the comparison of step (3), the
structure map of `(g, g^♯)` followed by the isomorphism of direct images which that datum produces
is the structure map of `(f_{small}, f_{small}^♯)`.

This is the source's closing paragraph.  Both sides are morphisms of sheaves on the small étale
site of `Y`; restriction to the small affine étale site is faithful ([Stacks Project, Tag 04HR]),
the restriction of the isomorphism of direct images is the one it was built from
(`MorphismOfTopoi.map_pushforwardIsoSheafPushforwardContinuousOfDenseSubsite_hom_app`), and at an
affine chart the equality on sections is
`AlgebraicGeometry.sectionsEquivOfIso_forgetFSharp`. -/
theorem forgetFSharp_comp_pushforwardIsoOfAffineRepresentableComparison
    (α : AffineRepresentableComparison B g f)
    (hα : ∀ V₀ : SmallAffineEtale B Y.obj Y.property,
      α.hom.app V₀ = affineComparisonSheafHom B g f hf V₀) :
    RingedToposHom.forgetFSharp g ≫
        (pushforwardIsoOfAffineRepresentableComparison B g f α).hom.app
          ((RingedSite.toRingedTopos
            (smallEtaleRingedSite B X.obj X.property)).forgetRing.obj
            (RingedSite.toRingedTopos
              (smallEtaleRingedSite B X.obj X.property)).O) =
      RingedToposHom.forgetFSharp (smallEtaleRingedToposHom B f) := by
  refine (SmallAffineEtale.restriction B Y.obj Y.property (Type u)).map_injective ?_
  have hmap : (SmallAffineEtale.restriction B Y.obj Y.property (Type u)).map
        ((pushforwardIsoOfAffineRepresentableComparison B g f α).hom.app
          ((RingedSite.toRingedTopos
            (smallEtaleRingedSite B X.obj X.property)).forgetRing.obj
            (RingedSite.toRingedTopos
              (smallEtaleRingedSite B X.obj X.property)).O)) =
      (MorphismOfTopoi.pushforwardRestrictionIsoSheafPushforwardContinuous g.toToposHom
          (SmallAffineEtale.topology B Y.obj Y.property) α).hom.app
        ((RingedSite.toRingedTopos
          (smallEtaleRingedSite B X.obj X.property)).forgetRing.obj
          (RingedSite.toRingedTopos
            (smallEtaleRingedSite B X.obj X.property)).O) :=
    MorphismOfTopoi.map_pushforwardIsoSheafPushforwardContinuousOfDenseSubsite_hom_app
      g.toToposHom (SmallAffineEtale.topology B Y.obj Y.property) α _
  rw [Functor.map_comp, hmap]
  refine Sheaf.hom_ext_sections fun V₀ b => ?_
  have := V₀.unop.property
  exact sectionsEquivOfIso_forgetFSharp B g f hf V₀.unop.obj (α.app V₀.unop)
    ((hα V₀.unop).trans (affineComparisonSheafHom_eq B g f hf V₀.unop)) b

include hf in
/-- **The existence half of [Stacks Project, Tag 04I6], with the source's own choice of `f`.**
For `(g, g^♯)` a morphism of the small étale *locally* ringed topoi and `f` the morphism of schemes
whose ring map on global functions is the one `g^♯` induces, `(g, g^♯)` is 2-isomorphic to
`(f_{small}, f_{small}^♯)`.

The 2-isomorphism is assembled from the comparison datum
`AlgebraicGeometry.affineRepresentableComparison` and the agreement of the two structure maps
above. -/
def twoIsoOfIsLocallyRinged (hg : g.IsLocallyRinged) :
    RingedToposHom.TwoIso.{u, u + 1, u, u, u + 1, u} g (smallEtaleRingedToposHom B f) :=
  twoIsoOfPushforwardIso B g f
    (pushforwardIsoOfAffineRepresentableComparison B g f
      (affineRepresentableComparison B g f hf hg))
    (forgetFSharp_comp_pushforwardIsoOfAffineRepresentableComparison B g f hf
      (affineRepresentableComparison B g f hf hg) fun _ => rfl)

/-- **The existence half of [Stacks Project, Tag 04I6].**  Let `X` and `Y` be schemes of a big
étale site with `Y` affine, and let

`(g, g^♯) : (Sh(X_étale), 𝒪_X) ⟶ (Sh(Y_étale), 𝒪_Y)`

be a morphism of *locally* ringed topoi.  Then there is a morphism of schemes `f : X ⟶ Y` such
that `(g, g^♯)` is 2-isomorphic to `(f_{small}, f_{small}^♯)` in the sense of
[Stacks Project, Tag 04IC].

This is the half of the tag that has content; uniqueness is
`AlgebraicGeometry.eq_of_twoIso_smallEtaleRingedToposHom`, i.e. [Stacks Project, Tag 04LW], and
needs no hypothesis, so it upgrades this to the `∃!` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.existsUnique_schemeHom_twoIso_of_isLocallyRinged` for free.  The affineness of
`X`, which the tag assumes, is not needed; see the module documentation. -/
@[stacks 04I6 "the existence clause: 2-isomorphic to some (f_small, f_small^sharp)"]
theorem exists_schemeHom_twoIso_of_isLocallyRinged (hg : g.IsLocallyRinged) :
    ∃ a : X ⟶ Y,
      Nonempty (RingedToposHom.TwoIso.{u, u + 1, u, u, u + 1, u} g
        (smallEtaleRingedToposHom B a)) :=
  have ⟨f, hf⟩ := exists_schemeHom_appTop_eq_globalSectionsMap B g
  ⟨f, ⟨twoIsoOfIsLocallyRinged B g f hf hg⟩⟩

/-- **[Stacks Project, Tag 04I6].**  Let `X` and `Y` be schemes of a big étale site with `Y`
affine, and let

`(g, g^♯) : (Sh(X_étale), 𝒪_X) ⟶ (Sh(Y_étale), 𝒪_Y)`

be a morphism of *locally* ringed topoi.  Then there is a **unique** morphism of schemes
`f : X ⟶ Y` such that `(g, g^♯)` is 2-isomorphic to `(f_{small}, f_{small}^♯)` in the sense of
[Stacks Project, Tag 04IC].

Existence is `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_schemeHom_twoIso_of_isLocallyRinged`, whose content is the
whole of the source's proof: the ring map on global functions and the morphism `f = Spec φ` it
names, the comparison `g⁻¹h_V ≅ h_{X ×_Y V}` at the affine étale charts of `Y` with its stalk
computation through [Stacks Project, Tag 04GX], the transport to all charts along
[Stacks Project, Tag 04HR], and the agreement of the two structure maps.  Uniqueness is
[Stacks Project, Tag 04LW], `AlgebraicGeometry.eq_of_twoIso_smallEtaleRingedToposHom`.

The tag assumes `X` affine as well; that hypothesis is not needed here. -/
@[stacks 04I6]
theorem existsUnique_schemeHom_twoIso_of_isLocallyRinged (hg : g.IsLocallyRinged) :
    ∃! a : X ⟶ Y,
      Nonempty (RingedToposHom.TwoIso.{u, u + 1, u, u, u + 1, u} g
        (smallEtaleRingedToposHom B a)) :=
  have ⟨a, ⟨t⟩⟩ := exists_schemeHom_twoIso_of_isLocallyRinged B g hg
  ⟨a, ⟨t⟩, fun b hb => eq_of_twoIso_smallEtaleRingedToposHom B g b a hb.some t⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
